    "instruction": "Could you open the CDC Child and Teen BMI Calculator. Use US Customary Units, enter Girl age 12 years 0 months, 5 ft 0 in, 120 lbs, then calculate. Copy results to Spreadsheet: B2=<BMI>, C2=<BMI Category>, D2=<BMI Percentile>. Set E2 to `=ABS(B2-20)`; use E2 as `Distance from 20`. In Prozilla OS, create the target text file and write sheet values in the format 'Scenario: Girl age 12 years 0 months, 5 ft 0 in, 120 lbs | BMI: <from sheet> | BMI Percentile: <from sheet> | Category: <from sheet> | Distance from 20: <from sheet>'.",
